        ]
      },
      "worked": "Let $X$ and $Y$ be the numbers on the first and second cards. With replacement, there are $20\\times20=400$ equally likely ordered pairs. Exactly 20 have equal numbers. Swapping the two draws pairs each outcome with $X>Y$ with an outcome with $X<Y$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}P(X>Y)&=\\frac{400-20}{2\\times400}\\\\P(X>Y)&=\\frac{19}{40}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
